  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN. You want to find an integer that is not present in the array AAA.\n\nUnfortunately, you only know addition of 222 numbers. So you will try to find an integer of the form X=Ai+AjX = A_i + A_jX=Ai​+Aj​ (1≤i,j≤N1 \\le i, j \\le N1≤i,j≤N), such that XXX does not appear in the array AAA.\n\nIf it is possible to find such an integer, print AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​. Here, AiA_iAi​ may be equal to AjA_jAj​, and even iii may be equal to jjj. If it is not possible, print −1-1−1.\n\nIf multiple answers are possible, all will be accepted.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​, the values chosen if it is possible, otherwise −1-1−1.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\le A_i \\le 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6\n2\n-5 5\n3\n4 -3 1\n1\n5\n3\n0 0 0\n3\n-1 -1 -2\n3\n1 1 2",
        "output": "-5 5\n4 1\n5 5\n-1\n-1 -2\n1 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : In the first test case, you choose i=1,j=2i = 1, j = 2i=1,j=2 to get X=−5+5=0X = -5 + 5 = 0X=−5+5=0 which is not present in the array.\nTest Case 3 : You choose i=j=1i = j = 1i=j=1. X=10X = 10X=10 not present in the array."
      }
    ]
  },
